---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { supportEmail } from '../data/site';

export const prerender = true;
const updatedAt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', {
  dateStyle: 'long',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(new Date());
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy and data"
  description="How Shift Calendar stores shift schedules and how the Tini Apps website is delivered."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="page-width document-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Simple by design. Local by default.</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      This page describes how the current Shift Calendar app and this website
      handle data.
    </p>
    <p class="updated-line">Updated {updatedAt}</p>

    {!supportEmail && (
      <aside class="draft-notice" aria-label="Publication status">
        <strong>Pre-release notice</strong>
        <p>
          The privacy contact is not set yet. This page is not ready to serve as
          the app store privacy policy.
        </p>
      </aside>
    )}

    <div class="prose-block">
      <h2>Shift Calendar data</h2>
      <p>
        The app stores shift dates, shift types, optional work hours, optional
        notes, and your reminder preference in a local SQLite database on your
        device. The current app has no account, cloud sync, advertising, or
        analytics service. Tini Apps does not receive your roster from the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app uses roster information to show your calendar, upcoming shifts,
        monthly totals, and optional local reminders. Notes are not included in
        reminders and are not sent to Tini Apps.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app does not add separate field-level encryption. Keep sensitive
        information out of shift notes and use your device's security settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Reminders</h2>
      <p>
        If you enable reminders, the app schedules local notifications on your
        device. They contain the shift type, date, and start time, not your notes.
        Delivery is best effort and depends on device settings and operating-system behavior.
      </p>

      <h2>Exports and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        CSV export is started by you and passed to the operating-system share
        sheet. The destination you select may make its own copy. Delete All
        Shifts removes roster records from the app; it cannot remove copies you
        have exported. Device backups are controlled by your operating system.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can view and edit your shifts in the app and delete the saved roster
        in Settings. Tini Apps cannot retrieve or erase roster data stored only
        on your device. For questions about this website or privacy practices,
        contact us using the address below.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no account, form, advertising, or analytics code. It is
        delivered through Cloudflare, which may process technical request data
        to operate and protect the service. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      {supportEmail ? (
        <p>For privacy questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.</p>
      ) : (
        <p>The public privacy and support contact is being confirmed.</p>
      )}
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
